   syntax: #alias [{name}] [{expansion}]
   With no arguments, #alias simply prints out all the aliases for the 
   current session.  With one argument, it prints out the aliases which 
   correspond to that pattern (wildcard * is supported).  Otherwise it 
   creates an alias for 'name' which will expand to 'expansion'.  Braces 
   are advised around both 'name' and 'expansion'.

   You can use pattern variables which look like % and a number.
   (ex: %4).  %0 is the entire text.  %n (where n is a number)
   is the nth item after the alias name.
   
   See also: unalias
